---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Writing | Evan Hobson" description="Essays by Evan Hobson.">
  <section class="page">
    <h1>Writing</h1>

    <div class="list">
      <article class="item">
        <h2><a href="/writing/permission-to-feel-power-to-become">Permission to Feel, Power to Become</a></h2>
        <p class="meta">Essay · BYU Student Religion Symposium</p>
        <p>
          On how Latter-day Saints treat the emotions that come with trials. I argue from scripture
          and emotion research that emotion is part of how people grow spiritually, not something
          faithful discipleship requires them to hold back.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="item">
        <h2>What God feels</h2>
        <p class="meta">In progress</p>
        <p>
          A longer project that grows out of the essay. It asks which emotions scripture attributes
          to God, with each emotion defined carefully enough to compare across passages. The
          categories describe how well we know something from the text. God is never scored.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
